            <ArticleTitle>An overview of pharmacology and acute pain: part one.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This two-part article, the fourth in a series on pain, explores the four main divisions of pharmacology: pharmacodynamics--what the medicine does to the body; pharmacokinetics--what the body does to the medicine; pharmacoeconomics--the cost and benefit ratio compared to other treatments; and pharmacovigilance--a medicine's safety profile. Part two, which will published next week, will explore the main categories of analgesic medicines.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
